.TH KEMPT 1 "2026-08-25" "Kempt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kempt \- one-click system updates for Fedora, from the terminal or the Plasma panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kempt
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B kempt check
.br
.B kempt update
.RB [ \-\-no\-flatpak ]
.RB [ \-\-surface=\c
.IR surface ]
.br
.B kempt run
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B kempt summary
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B kempt summary \-\-json
.br
.B kempt history
.br
.B kempt log
.RB [ \-n
.IR N ]
.br
.B kempt doctor
.br
.B kempt hold
.IR backend : name
.br
.B kempt unhold
.IR backend : name
.br
.B kempt holds
.br
.B kempt config get
.I key
.RI [ default ]
.br
.B kempt config set
.I key value
.br
.B kempt enable\-passwordless
.br
.B kempt disable\-passwordless
.br
.B kempt \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kempt
reports and applies pending system updates from the dnf5 and Flatpak backends, and is the
engine behind the Kempt Plasma panel widget. It queries the same root metadata cache that the
update itself uses, so the pending count and the update can never disagree.
.PP
Packages can be
.B held:
excluded from every Kempt run while still being reported as pending. When a pending
transaction touches session\-critical packages such as the kernel, systemd or the Qt and KDE
stack, an interactive run recommends staging the transaction for the next reboot instead of
rewriting a running desktop.
.PP
Only two small helpers run as root, one per polkit action, and both validate every argument
before executing anything. Both belong to the dnf side. Flatpak updates run as you:
.BR flatpak (1)
grants a system app update to an active local session without a password, so a run with nothing
but Flatpak updates in it never raises an authentication dialog.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
Query every enabled backend, write the state file and print it as JSON. Takes no arguments.
Backend failures do not fail the command: the state is marked
.B stale
with an error message and the previous item lists are kept. Empty output with exit status 0
means "no data, keep the last known state", never "zero updates". This command also harvests a
staged offline transaction once the machine has rebooted, and refreshes package metadata at most
once every three hours, never on battery or on a metered connection.
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-no\-flatpak "] [" \-\-surface= \c
.IR surface ]
Run the update now. Options come from the configuration file;
.B \-\-no\-flatpak
excludes Flatpak apps for this run and
.B \-\-surface=
overrides the run surface
.RB ( terminal ", " popup ", " background ", " offline ).
An unrecognized surface falls back to
.BR terminal .
Held items are excluded and listed. When session\-critical packages are pending, an interactive
terminal run first offers to update live, stage the transaction offline, or abort; anything
other than an explicit yes aborts, having changed nothing.
.TP
.BR run " [" \-\-dry\-run ]
Launch
.B kempt update
according to the configured surface and return immediately. This is what the widget's Update Now
button calls.
.B \-\-dry\-run
prints what would be launched.
A successful launch says nothing about the update's outcome: poll the state file or the history.
.TP
.BR summary " [" \c
.IR N ]
Render one run as human\-readable text.
.I N
counts back from the newest and defaults to 1. Corrupt entries are skipped with a warning.
.TP
.B summary \-\-json
Print the newest run's history entry verbatim as JSON, and nothing else. The entry is validated
before any of it is printed, and a damaged newest entry falls back to the next\-newest with a
warning on stderr. Takes no
.IR N .
With no runs recorded, or with every entry damaged, it prints nothing and exits 0: empty output
means "no data", never an empty run.
.TP
.B history
List past runs, newest first: timestamp, surface, status and what the run changed. The last
column counts upgrades, installs and removals in the same words the notifications use
.RB ( "3 updated, +1 installed" ", " "no package changes" ),
so a run that only installed or removed packages is never listed as "0 updated".
.TP
.BR log " [" \-n " " \c
.IR N ]
Print the event log, oldest of the shown lines first.
.I N
defaults to 30. Each line is
.IR "timestamp via text" ,
where
.I via
is
.B widget
when the command came from the Plasma widget and
.B cli
for anything else, and the text comes from a fixed vocabulary: config changes with the value
they replaced, holds, check outcomes with their counts, metadata refreshes, run start and run
result, offline staging, harvests and passwordless attempts. With nothing recorded yet it prints
.B "No events recorded yet."
and exits 0. This is the file to read when the question is "did the change I just made land?",
which the per-run logs and the history cannot answer.
.TP
.B doctor
Check this installation and print one line per check, prefixed
.BR ok ", " info " or " FAIL :
both root helpers at the polkit\-annotated paths and owned by root, the polkit action file,
.BR jq ,
the terminal emulator, flatpak, the configuration file's syntax, a writable state directory and
an intact checkout. Every check runs even after one fails. Exit status 1 when anything failed.
The last five lines of the event log are printed after the checks; they are not a check and never
affect the exit status.
.IP
The report ends with the install itself. A
.B version:
line names the release, and in a git checkout the commit it came from and whether the tree is
clean. Then
.BR helpers: ", " policy: " and " widget:
compare each installed copy against the checkout, byte for byte: the CLI is a symlink, so
.B git pull
updates it at once, while the two root helpers, the polkit action and the widget package are
copies that change only when
.B ./install.sh
runs.
.B DIFFER
means exactly that pull, and the line names the command that fixes it. An install that did not
come from a checkout prints
.B "install: packaged"
and compares nothing, because the package manager keeps those files in step.
Worth running when
.B check
reports nothing pending on a machine that cannot possibly be up to date: a missing root helper
leaves
.B check
exiting 0 with a
.B stale
state and no items.
.TP
.BI hold " backend:name"
Exclude a package or app from Kempt runs while still reporting it as pending.
.I backend
is
.B dnf
or
.BR flatpak ;
the colon is required. Holds are Kempt's own list, not a system\-wide version lock.
.TP
.BI unhold " backend:name"
Remove a hold. Removing one that does not exist is not an error.
.TP
.B holds
List current holds, one
.I backend:name
per line.
.TP
.BI "config get" " key " [ default ]
Print a configuration value, falling back to the built\-in default for the key, or to
.I default
if given.
.TP
.BI "config set" " key value"
Set a configuration value. Keys must match
.RB ' ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]+$ '
and values must be single\-line.
.TP
.B enable\-passwordless
Install a polkit rule that lets the current user apply updates without the authentication
dialog. It covers one action id only, for that user, and only in an active local session -
the dnf half, which is the only half that ever asks, since Flatpak app updates already run
without a prompt.
.TP
.B disable\-passwordless
Remove that rule.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " version ", " \-V
Print
.RB ' "kempt <version>" '
and exit. The version is read from the
.I VERSION
file in the checkout, which is the project's single source of truth for it; a checkout without
one prints
.RB ' "kempt unknown" '
rather than failing, because a build that cannot say what it is must still be able to update the
machine.
.BR "kempt doctor" 's
first line reports the same version and the checkout it came from.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings live in
.I ~/.config/kempt/config
as
.IR key = value
lines and are read and written with
.BR "kempt config" .
The keys are
.BR include_flatpak " (default " true "),"
.BR auto_accept " (default " true "),"
.BR surface " (default " terminal "),"
.BR refresh_interval_min " (default " 60 "),"
.BR widget_icon_size " (default " auto "),"
.BR restart_reminder " (default " true ") and"
.BR risky_regex .
A value counts as true when it is
.BR true ", " 1 " or " yes ;
everything else is false.
.PP
.B restart_reminder
governs the Plasma widget's popup only: with it on, a popup opened while a restart is owed shows a
message saying so and offers a button that opens KDE's own restart prompt; with it off there is no
message and no button, and the popup's status line still ends
.BR "restart pending" .
Nothing ever restarts on its own either way.
.PP
See
.I docs/configuration.md
in the source tree for the full reference.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <checkout>/VERSION
The project's version, and the single source of truth for it: the widget's
.I metadata.json
is pinned to this file by the test suite, and a release's tag, RPM version and AppStream release
are expected to agree with it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kempt/config
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kempt/holds
Holds, one
.I backend:name
per line.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/state.json
Latest check result, schema v1. A documented public interface.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/history/
One JSON entry per run. The newest 50 are kept.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/logs/
Full raw output per run. Deleted after 60 days. Evidence, never rewritten: a failure that a
summary reports as
.B "authentication declined or cancelled"
appears here in the authentication helper's own words.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/events.log
The event log, mode 0600. One line per thing Kempt did. Past 2500 lines it is rewritten to the
last 2000; nothing else deletes from it.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/kempt-refresh
Root helper: package metadata only, no authentication dialog.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/kempt-apply
Root helper: the dnf upgrade verbs, one authentication per run.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.erez_c137.kempt.policy
The two polkit actions.
.TP
.I /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/49-kempt.rules
Present only while passwordless mode is enabled.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/io.github.erez_c137.kempt/
The Plasma panel widget, installed by
.B install.sh
with
.BR kpackagetool6 .
Unlike the CLI it is a copy, not a symlink, so re-run
.B install.sh
after changing it. Installing it does not add it to a panel; that is Add Widgets.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/apps/kempt.svg
The widget's icon, in the user's icon theme, which is how its name resolves in Add Widgets.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including declining at the session\-critical recommendation prompt.
.TP
.B 1
The run itself failed (a backend returned non\-zero), or
.B doctor
found at least one problem.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, option or argument.
.TP
.B 3
Cannot start: jq is missing, or another
.B kempt update
holds the lock.
.TP
.B 4
Launcher missing: no terminal emulator for the
.B terminal
surface.
.TP
.B 5
Aborted during pre\-flight. Nothing was changed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnf5 (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
Full documentation in the source tree:
.IR README.md ", " docs/usage.md ", " docs/configuration.md ", " docs/architecture.md
and
.IR docs/security.md .
